Here's a simple JavaScript function that accepts text and posts a message via the Slack API to the specified channel:

```javascript
function postMessageToSlack(text, channel) {
  const webhookUrl = `https://hooks.slack.com/services/${process.env.SLACK_APP_ID}/B${process.env.SLACK_APP_TOKEN}/${channel}`;

  fetch(webhookUrl, {
    method: 'POST',
    headers: {
      'Content-Type': 'application/json'
    },
    body: JSON.stringify({
      text: text
    })
  })
    .then(response => response.json())
    .catch(error => console.error(error));
}
```

Make sure you have set up your Slack app and obtained the necessary environment variables (`SLACK_APP_ID` and `SLACK_APP_TOKEN`) for the webhook URL. You can call this function with the desired text and channel like this:

```javascript
postMessageToSlack('Hello, world!', '#general');
```

This will send the message "Hello, world!" to the specified channel in your Slack workspace.

